      ],
      "title": "Consciousness & Computation",
      "gist": "Seth lays out four arguments—that brains aren't computers, that other non-computational dynamics may matter, that life itself may be necessary, and that simulation isn't instantiation—to show that computational functionalism, and hence conscious AI, rests on shaky ground.",
      "sourceHeading": "Consciousness & Computation"
    },
